oked with","count":1,"groups":[["Argentine cuisine","cuisine/argentine-cuisine",[["Rogel (cake)","dish/rogel-cake"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Dulce de leche","ingredient/dulce-de-leche"],["Puff pastry","ingredient/puff-pastry"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/19/Meringues_9027.jpg/500px-Meringues_9027.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Mike Lehmann, Mike Switzerland 12:44, 27 January 2007 (UTC)","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Meringues_9027.jpg"}},"ingredient/cucurbita-pepo":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/cucurbita-pepo","n":"Cucurbita pepo","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Cucurbita pepo is a cultivated plant of the genus Cucurbita. It yields varieties of winter squash and pumpkin, but the most widespread varieties belong to the subspecies Cucurbita pepo subsp. pepo, called summer squash."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-cucurbita-pepo"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cucurbita_pepo"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Andorran cuisine","cuisine/andorran-cuisine",[["Samfaina","dish/samfaina"]]],["Catalan cuisine","cuisine/catalan-cuisine",[["Samfaina","dish/samfaina"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Eggplant","ingredient/eggplant"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/a6/Cucurbita_pepo_collage_1.png/500px-Cucurbita_pepo_collage_1.png","w":500,"h":414,"by":"Various","lic":"CC BY-SA 1.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/1.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cucurbita_pepo_collage_1.png"}},"dish/sencha":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/sencha","n":"Sencha","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Japanese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Sencha is a type of Japanese green tea (緑茶, ryokucha) which is prepared by infusing the processed whole tea leaves in hot water. This is as opposed to matcha (抹茶), powdered Japanese green tea, where the green tea powder is mixed with hot water and therefore the leaf itself is included in the beverage. Sencha is the most popular tea in Japan."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-sencha"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sencha"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Bancha","ingredient/bancha"],["Gyokuro","ingredient/gyokuro"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Just One Cookbook","ref":"site/justonecookbook-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"justonecookbook.com","note":"Namiko Chen's long-running blog and videos on Japanese home cooking.","url":"https://justonecookbook.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"RecipeTin Japan","ref":"site/japan-recipetineats-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"japan.recipetineats.com","note":"Japanese home recipes from Yumiko, a Japan-born cook, sister site to RecipeTin Eats.","url":"https://japan.recipetineats.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Japanese cuisine","links":[["Bergh–Stoutenburgh House","dish/bergh-stoutenburgh-house"],["Chikuwa","dish/chikuwa"],["Curry bread","dish/curry-bread"],["Donburi","dish/donburi"],["Fukamushicha","dish/fukamushicha"],["Gyokuro","dish/gyokuro"],["Hitsumabushi","dish/hitsumabushi"],["Horumonyaki","dish/horumonyaki"],["Iekei ramen","dish/iekei-ramen"],["Inago no tsukudani","dish/inago-no-tsukudani"],["Itamae","dish/itamae"],["Izakaya","dish/izakaya"],["Japanese cheesecake","dish/japanese-cheesecake"],["Japanese noodles","dish/japanese-noodles"],["Japanese restaurant","dish/japanese-restaurant"],["Japanese tea","dish/japanese-tea"],["Jingisukan","dish/jingisukan"],["Kaki furai","dish/kaki-furai"],["Kamaboko","dish/kam